{"metadata":{"externalID":"s:8AxiamSDK0A6ClientC21resendOwnVerificationyyYaKF","symbolKind":"method","role":"symbol","fragments":[{"kind":"keyword","text":"func"},{"kind":"text","text":" "},{"kind":"identifier","text":"resendOwnVerification"},{"kind":"text","text":"() "},{"kind":"keyword","text":"async"},{"kind":"text","text":" "},{"kind":"keyword","text":"throws"}],"roleHeading":"Instance Method","title":"resendOwnVerification()","extendedModule":"AxiamSDK","modules":[{"name":"AxiamSDK"}]},"hierarchy":{"paths":[["doc:\/\/AxiamSDK\/documentation\/AxiamSDK","doc:\/\/AxiamSDK\/documentation\/AxiamSDK\/AxiamClient"]]},"kind":"symbol","schemaVersion":{"patch":0,"minor":3,"major":0},"variants":[{"paths":["\/documentation\/axiamsdk\/axiamclient\/resendownverification()"],"traits":[{"interfaceLanguage":"swift"}]}],"primaryContentSections":[{"declarations":[{"tokens":[{"kind":"keyword","text":"func"},{"kind":"text","text":" "},{"kind":"identifier","text":"resendOwnVerification"},{"kind":"text","text":"() "},{"kind":"keyword","text":"async"},{"kind":"text","text":" "},{"kind":"keyword","text":"throws"}],"platforms":["Linux"],"languages":["swift"]}],"kind":"declarations"},{"kind":"content","content":[{"type":"heading","text":"Discussion","level":2,"anchor":"discussion"},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Takes no address. The server reads it off the caller’s own record, and this signature"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"deliberately offers no way to name a different one: a parameter here would let an"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"authenticated session mail an arbitrary address."}]},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Unlike "},{"type":"reference","isActive":true,"identifier":"doc:\/\/AxiamSDK\/documentation\/AxiamSDK\/AxiamClient\/resendVerification(email:tenantID:)"},{"type":"text","text":" this reports the outcome, because the"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"caller is signed in to the account it is asking about and none of the outcomes tells"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"it anything it did not already bring with it:"}]},{"items":[{"content":[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"returns — a token was minted and the mail "},{"type":"strong","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"enqueued"}]},{"type":"text","text":". Delivery is asynchronous"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"and can still fail at the provider; a queue that accepts everything in front of a"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"provider that rejects it looks exactly like this succeeding (§25.7 rule 3)."}]}]},{"content":[{"inlineContent":[{"type":"codeVoice","code":"AxiamError.authz"},{"type":"text","text":" (from "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"409"},{"type":"text","text":") — already verified, or an account state that must"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"not be sent a live token."}],"type":"paragraph"}]},{"content":[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"code":"AxiamError.network","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" (from ","type":"text"},{"code":"429","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":") — the daily resend limit.","type":"text"}]}]}],"type":"unorderedList"},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"§25.7 rule 2 forbids falling back to the unauthenticated endpoint on either failure,"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"and this SDK does not: that fallback turns both back into a silent success and"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"restores the bug this operation exists to fix, with an extra round trip."}]},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Refused client-side with "},{"type":"strong","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"no wire call"}]},{"type":"text","text":" when there is no session."}]}]}],"abstract":[{"code":"POST \/api\/v1\/users\/me\/resend-verification","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":" (CONTRACT.md §25.1, §25.7) — resend the"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"strong","inlineContent":[{"text":"signed-in caller’s own","type":"text"}]},{"type":"text","text":" verification mail, and say what happened."}],"sections":[],"identifier":{"interfaceLanguage":"swift","url":"doc:\/\/AxiamSDK\/documentation\/AxiamSDK\/AxiamClient\/resendOwnVerification()"},"references":{"doc://AxiamSDK/documentation/AxiamSDK":{"role":"collection","title":"AxiamSDK","abstract":[{"text":"The official Swift SDK for AXIAM (Access eXtended Identity and Authorization Management).","type":"text"}],"kind":"symbol","type":"topic","url":"\/documentation\/axiamsdk","identifier":"doc:\/\/AxiamSDK\/documentation\/AxiamSDK"},"doc://AxiamSDK/documentation/AxiamSDK/AxiamClient/resendOwnVerification()":{"identifier":"doc:\/\/AxiamSDK\/documentation\/AxiamSDK\/AxiamClient\/resendOwnVerification()","title":"resendOwnVerification()","type":"topic","url":"\/documentation\/axiamsdk\/axiamclient\/resendownverification()","kind":"symbol","role":"symbol","abstract":[{"code":"POST \/api\/v1\/users\/me\/resend-verification","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" (CONTRACT.md §25.1, §25.7) — resend the","type":"text"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"signed-in caller’s own"}],"type":"strong"},{"type":"text","text":" verification mail, and say what happened."}],"fragments":[{"kind":"keyword","text":"func"},{"kind":"text","text":" "},{"kind":"identifier","text":"resendOwnVerification"},{"kind":"text","text":"() "},{"kind":"keyword","text":"async"},{"kind":"text","text":" "},{"kind":"keyword","text":"throws"}]},"doc://AxiamSDK/documentation/AxiamSDK/AxiamClient/resendVerification(email:tenantID:)":{"title":"resendVerification(email:tenantID:)","identifier":"doc:\/\/AxiamSDK\/documentation\/AxiamSDK\/AxiamClient\/resendVerification(email:tenantID:)","abstract":[{"code":"POST \/api\/v1\/auth\/resend-verification","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" (CONTRACT.md §25.1) — the","type":"te